7 0 obj
<< /Length 1912 >>
stream
BT /F1 12 Tf 50 780 Td 16 TL
(The water was the colour of an old spoon. Across it, a low line of land appeared) Tj T*
(and disappeared in the mist.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(I sat on a wall that had been repaired with three different kinds of stone. The) Tj T*
(repairs were not hidden. Each had its own colour, its own idea of a straight edge.) Tj T*
(Together they held up the wall.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A person came down to the water with an empty bucket. They filled it, stood for a) Tj T*
(moment, and carried it away. I do not know why. There are still many things I do) Tj T*
(not need to know.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The tide moved a small piece of wood up the beach, then down again. For ten) Tj T*
(minutes it seemed to make no progress. Then I looked away and the wood was gone.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(IV. THE ROOM) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(At the end of the day, the room has changed. The furniture is where it was, but) Tj T*
(the light has moved everything a little to the left.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(There is a book open on the table. There is a cup beside it. Neither is waiting in) Tj T*
(any dramatic sense. They are simply available.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(I like that word. Available. Something offered without insistence.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Perhaps that is what a library should be: not a list of things to finish, but a) Tj T*
(room full of things that are available. A story for one kind of afternoon. A song) Tj T*
(for another. A window when the words will not come.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(I close the notebook. Outside, the unnamed tree is becoming a shape against the) Tj T*
(sky. Tomorrow I may look up its name. Tonight, it is enough to notice that it is) Tj T*
(there.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(END) Tj T*
